+# HANDOFF — Pending work to push (not yet on GitHub)
+
+**Status:** All work below is complete, tested, and committed locally as `b04bf2b` on branch `arena/01a0327b-ghatnachakra-bpsc`. It could NOT be pushed because the previous session closed (its PR #12 was merged). This sandbox's `origin/main` is a pre-merge clone, so do not trust its refs — fetch fresh.
+
+**What's already on GitHub (merged via PR #12):** attempt-history details + Retry Wrong / Retry Skipped.
+
+**What's pending here (the new PR to create):**
+1. **Sub-topics for all 15 KGS test papers** — `topic` tag on every question (`scripts/tag_test_topics.js` + `scripts/topic_rules.js`, run `node scripts/tag_test_topics.js` to re-tag). Topic chips inside each test card (tap = practice that topic only), topic pill on quiz/review/bank items, topic-wise ✓/✗/— performance table on the result screen and in History → Details.
+2. **⬇ Export PDF on Mistakes & Skips screens** — A4 black & white print sheet (question, options, correct answer marked, user's wrong answer flagged, full explanation) via hidden iframe + print dialog. Respects active filters.
+3. `server.js` — tiny no-cache static preview server.
+
+## How to ship it (next session)
+
+```bash
+git fetch origin
+git checkout -b <new-session-branch> origin/main   # main already has PR #12
+# Copy the 21 files listed in handoff/changed-files.txt from the preserved
+# workspace over the checkout (they contain PR-12 changes + the new work,
+# so a straight copy is safe and conflict-free), OR:
+git apply --3way handoff/full-work.patch   # PR-12 hunks already match; if
+# any fail because already applied, that is expected — use the file-copy route.
+npm install && npm test                     # suite must PASS
+git add -A && git commit && git push origin <new-session-branch>
+# then open the PR to main.
+```
+
+Verification already done in the prior session: `npm test` PASS (includes new
+coverage: topic chips/practice/pills/breakdown + PDF export), full jsdom
+simulation of a 150-Q Bihar Special test (20%, ✓30 ✗39 —81) with 17-topic
+breakdown table, and a real buildBankExportHtml A4 sheet.
+
+Do not re-run the tagger against already-tagged files expecting different
+output — it is idempotent and order/uid-preserving (attempt history safety).
