+for this repo that must be shipped as a PR. Do exactly this:
+
+1. Save the attached file as `full-work.patch` in the repo root.
+2. The patch is based on commit `d9b377b` (an ancestor of main, exists on
+   GitHub) and applies 100% cleanly there — verified. Run:
+
+   ```bash
+   git fetch origin
+   git checkout -b topics-pdf-export d9b377b
+   git apply full-work.patch        # must apply with no errors
+   npm install && npm test          # suite must print "status": "PASS"
+   git add -A
+   git commit -m "Sub-topics for all 15 test papers + A4 Export PDF for Mistakes/Skips"
+   # pull in current main (already has PR #12); identical hunks auto-resolve:
+   git merge origin/main -m "Merge main"     # should auto-merge cleanly
+   git push origin topics-pdf-export
+   gh pr create --base main --head topics-pdf-export \
+     --title "Sub-topics in all 15 test papers + Export PDF (A4) for Mistakes/Skips" \
+     --body-file -  <<'PRBODY'
+   ## What this adds
+   - **Sub-topics for all 15 KGS test papers**: every question gets a `topic` tag
+     (Bihar Special -> Ancient/Medieval/Modern Bihar, Rivers & Lakes, Minerals,
+     Census & Population...; Bio -> Cell/Genetics/Physiology...; Phy+Chem ->
+     Optics/Sound/Motion/Metals...). Tap a topic chip inside a test card to
+     practice only that topic; topic pill on questions, review and bank lists;
+     topic-wise performance table (Q / correct / wrong / skip / score) on the
+     result screen and in History -> Details.
+   - **Export PDF** button on Mistakes and Skips screens: print-ready A4
+     black & white sheet with question, options, correct answer marked,
+     user's wrong answer flagged, and the full explanation. Respects filters.
+   - `server.js`: no-cache static preview server. `scripts/tag_test_topics.js`
+     + `scripts/topic_rules.js`: idempotent offline topic tagger.
+   - Tests extended and passing (topic chips/practice/pills/breakdown, PDF export).
+   PRBODY
+   ```
